IMMUTABLE MEANS THE CONTENT NEVER CHANGES, NOT THAT IT CAN NEVER BE REMOVED.
Those are two different acts and one word was doing both (settled 2026-10-23):

    CORRECT IT   a new version. Always. A published version's files are never
                 rewritten, because a build may have been tested against them
                 and "the version I tested" has to stay true.

    WITHDRAW IT  deletion, and a last resort rather than maintenance. Decided
                 2026-10-02: admin may do it, behind deliberately heavy
                 friction. NOT BUILT.

The PDF permission table says "admin: read/write/delete" on a published
version, which conflates them. Read it as "read, and may withdraw" — never
"may rewrite", which the same document forbids three sections later.
